implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST — the accepted append control, driven through the PRODUCTION seam, not by calling the service directly. Create apps/daemon/src/journal/journal-append.test.ts over a REAL SqliteEventStore and the real session authenticator, following the harness already used by apps/daemon/src/daemon-command-registry.test.ts (real ports via `createDaemonCommandPorts`/`createStoreDependencies`) plus the activation fixture pattern of apps/daemon/src/work/attempt-release-disposition.test.ts (`openHarnessStore`, `seedReadyProject`, and an activation minted ONLY by `runEffectActivateCommand` — a hand-forged activation cannot satisfy `parseActivationGrant`'s hex64 grantId, and this suite needs a genuinely BOUND attempt).
Write RED:
- one accepted `journal.append` with two entries: the command is DECIDED, and the durable reader returns both entries in canonical order with a lowercase hex64 `journalDigest`;
- empty-current-journal semantics: the FIRST append on an attempt with no prior journal succeeds and yields exactly the appended entries — an ABSENT current journal is the empty list here and is the ONLY place ABSENT is not fatal;
- the digest is the production surface's own: assert it equals `createDeadEndJournal(<the returned entries>).journal.digest` from `@moe/context`, never a hand-written 64-char literal.
Confirm the suite fails because the kind is unregistered, not because the harness is wrong.
